# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Flora .gitignore
#
# Rule of thumb: CODE, CONFIG and SKILLS are tracked. DATA and SECRETS are not.
# Everything ignored here is either regenerable (state/) or must never leave
# this machine (secrets/). To copy the platform elsewhere, copy the directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Live data. shared/ is Flora's brain -- skills, instructions, MCP servers -- and
# both agents WRITE to it, so it cannot live in the repository you pull the
# platform from: a `git pull` would collide with the platform's own data every
# time. The shipped defaults are in seed/ and `bin/flora seed` installs any that
# are missing, without ever overwriting a live file.
# To keep a history of your own skills, make shared/ its own repository:
#     git init shared && git -C shared add -A && git -C shared commit -m "skills"
/shared/

# Runtime state: agent sessions, databases, Mattermost volumes, caches.
/state/

# Secrets: API keys, bot tokens, passwords, htpasswd, ssh keys.
# The whole directory is excluded, so nothing inside it can be re-included --
# scripts/bootstrap-secrets.sh creates it, mode 0700, on a fresh clone.
/secrets/
*.key
*.pem
!config/templates/**/*.pem.tmpl

# The live, rendered config (contains the resolved values of flora.env).
/flora.env
/config/rendered/

# Repositories Flora clones and works in.
/workspace/*
!/workspace/.gitkeep

# Generated dashboard health data.
/web/dashboard/health.json

# Editors / OS noise.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
